      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It is not VRC but SteamVR that false inform game that headset is off when you open the menu (most likely in hope to trigger pause menu), same as it stops sending hand tracking information to the game (which you can see if you disable AFK), same as Oculus menu don't stop sending button and touch state information and put you to permanent \"Free hand\" gesture (to avoid incidentally triggering things). VRC can't do much here since it ha no information if head set is really off or not.\n \nI never touched SteamVR on dev side so i don't know if there way to detect menu or disable headset off state on menu, but even so VRC also depends on Unity implementation to SteamVR which may be extra barrier to do so.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
